    Episode, Download, Comments, Author, Title, ...): negative (about -0.08);
  - the chat-markup tag <tool_call> negative (-0.14), and </tool_response> positive (+0.13);
  - an ordinary lowercase English content word (with its leading space, not a function word):
    slightly positive (+0.004);
  - a capitalised word or a number at the start of a line (after a newline): slightly negative (-0.014);
  - everything else (function words, punctuation, spaces, code, CJK): near the mean, 0.
A constant baseline of 0.0024 (the component's mean) is added to every position.
Measured: it explains about 1-2% of the activation's variance; the component is mostly noise
at the token level, and no compact concept found explains more.
"""
READS = ()
FUNCTION_WORDS = frozenset("the of and a an to in is it that for on with as by at be this are was or from not but have has had they you we he she his her its their our your my i me them us do does did so if then than there here what which who when where how all any some no more most other such only own same too very can will would should could may might must just also into about over after before under between through during without within".split())
METADATA_LABELS = frozenset("Posts Posted Download Category Follow Joined Abstract Article Episode Editor Share Views Comments Author Title Chapter README Status Last Today Own Forum Topic Member Contents Description Introduction Summary Keywords Tags Email Home Search Menu".split())
