"""Approximate a negative response to the start of a quoted string.

Quotes fused to an opening brace or square bracket dominate; function-call
quotes are weaker, and escaped quotes weaker still. A separate quote is more
negative after code separators or indentation than after prose. Most other
tokens get zero; this is not a full string parser. Only the previous token is
kept, and it is reset at document boundaries. Constants are rounded
training-based estimates of each punctuation category's response.
